# quirc 1.2, lib/quirc.c: the first quirc_resize copies from a buffer that does not
# exist yet, with a length of zero. memcpy is declared with non-null arguments, so
# this is undefined by the letter of the standard and harmless in practice.
#
# Suppressed rather than fixed because vendored sources are not patched in place.
# Reported upstream shape: quirc_resize's "min" computation is correct; the call is
# simply made before there is anything to copy.
nonnull-attribute:quirc.c
